WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Welcome back.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.490
We are here with the stars
of the new movie, Air,

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.130
which is in theaters
starting starting April 5th.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.680
First of all,
congratulations, Ben, on Air.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.890
It is an incredible story
and it's interesting.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.800
I knew nothing about
Michael Jordan's start.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.600
I knew nothing about the
company- I knew nothing.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.470
And it is so informative
and funny and serious

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.510
and has real issues that you talk about,

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.343
as far as knowing your worth.

00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:23.910
- Well, that's interesting
'cause there are people who,

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.750
like definitely are kind of
not into sports or basketball

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:28.627
- That's like me, yeah.

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:30.018
- or sports movies or that kind of thing.

00:00:30.018 --> 00:00:31.517
Who are like, "See that's not my thing".

00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:33.840
But actually it's not that, it's really,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.400
it's not a rah-rah thing.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.800
It's not about like you
have to know the sport

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.777
and the locker room
and we're gonna win it.

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:42.360
It's about how this person, you know,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.360
Michael Jordan, meant so much to the world

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.480
and represented something
so big and so amazing.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.200
He kind of changed the way
the world perceived athletes

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.440
and the way they connected
Nike, in concert with him,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.520
kind of, it was the first
time you associated a product,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.353
a brand-

00:01:00.353 --> 00:01:01.295
- Yeah.

00:01:01.295 --> 00:01:02.160
- [Ben] With a person and their identity.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.010
Back then they were in the
cellar with basketball shoes.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:08.292
Converse was killing.
Adidas was the cool shoes.

00:01:08.292 --> 00:01:09.353
- I didn't know all that.

00:01:09.353 --> 00:01:10.186
- [Chris, Matt, and Ben] Yeah.

00:01:10.186 --> 00:01:11.202
- I know.

00:01:11.202 --> 00:01:12.480
- That was the weird thing,
reading the script was what-

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.250
I mean I just thought it
was such a great story

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.210
that I didn't know.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.398
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:01:16.398 --> 00:01:17.730
- And kinda at the beginning
of the movie did have to

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.890
re-contextualize that time, 'cause you go,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.200
we all live in the world
post Michael Jordan,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.751
post Air Jordan you know?

00:01:23.751 --> 00:01:24.584
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.890
- [Matt] So to take us
back to that time right

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.020
before it all happened and
what the world looked like,

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.220
and it's funny to think of Nike

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.660
as an underdog 'cause they're so-

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.493
- That's what I'm saying!

00:01:31.493 --> 00:01:33.120
And then knowing Adidas,
like, it was just-

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.220
it was an interesting thing
that I did not know about.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.760
Even how- I loved when you and
Viola Davis' character were

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.620
at her house and you were just going back

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.594
and forth about like what
to expect in those meetings.

00:01:43.594 --> 00:01:44.427
- (laughing) Right. Right.

00:01:44.427 --> 00:01:45.334
- [Kelly] They like play it out.

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:46.800
Like it was brilliant and it was funny,

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.560
but it was really honest as well.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.350
And it really showed how the
company really got behind-

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.570
I mean y'all literally
sank everything into like-

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.642
they sank everything into this one person.

00:01:56.642 --> 00:01:58.950
= Well, it seems like
an obvious thing now.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:01:59.783
- [Kelly] But not then.

00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:00.616
- But it was a real-

00:02:00.616 --> 00:02:02.040
it was a massive gamble that they-

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.200
- What I loved about it is,
as you mentioned, Viola-

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.242
is that you think it's really-

00:02:06.242 --> 00:02:07.075
well it's gonna be this
guy's Sonny's story,

00:02:07.075 --> 00:02:08.850
or it's gonna be Michael Jordan's story.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.680
And you get halfway through the movie,

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.210
which sort of mirrored the process I had

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:16.140
in exploring it and trying
to put together the cast

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.880
and the whole sort of ideas
that were important to me.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.280
And you find out really like

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.960
almost like I was almost embarrassed

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.941
that it wasn't obvious to begin with.

00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:27.420
That without Deloris Jordan, his mother-

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.408
- Yeah.

00:02:28.408 --> 00:02:29.640
- [Ben] Really guiding him and helping him

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.500
and making us do- none
of that would happen.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.640
And it just makes so much sense.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.100
Like all these moms, like
I think of my own mom.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.840
My mom loves all my movies,
you know what I mean?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.740
She thinks everything's great.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.710
I'm like, they're not all great, mom.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:40.543
But you know? God bless her.

00:02:40.543 --> 00:02:41.970
And nobody loves you like your mother.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.060
And the way that, especially young people

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.940
and the case of the NBA and entertainment,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.340
you see, they get thrust
into these positions.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.020
Sometimes they're from
marginalized communities,

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.850
they've historically
been taken advantage of,

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:54.900
and here they are with
these opportunities,

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.920
they're supposed to be negotiating

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.630
with these massive companies.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.294
It's a whole, you know,

00:02:59.294 --> 00:03:02.070
we know a little bit about
sort of stepping from one world

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.510
into another- it's a lot.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.790
And if you don't have that
person there to anchor you

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.440
and guide you might be in trouble.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.576
- And also though what you're saying is,

00:03:09.576 --> 00:03:10.409
seems a bit normalized now.

00:03:10.409 --> 00:03:11.968
People do fight for that now.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.980
But back then, like
even on the phone call,

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.780
you were like, oh ma'am you
don't know how this works.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.400
Like, that's not how it works.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.637
And she was basically like,

00:03:18.637 --> 00:03:21.161
"But this is how it's
going to, if you'd like

00:03:21.161 --> 00:03:24.377
to work with my-" and I
thought that was so powerful.

00:03:24.377 --> 00:03:26.311
- Because it's important
to understand the people

00:03:26.311 --> 00:03:27.330
that said, "No, there's a
difference between a salary

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.060
and a fee, and ownership.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:30.893
- Yeah.

00:03:30.893 --> 00:03:31.890
- And people, owners-

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.860
In other words, you go out
and you create the value

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.150
in the shoe by being Michael Jordan.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.130
Well, you're an owner of your identity

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.920
and you should own what
that means to this company.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.330
It's not like, "Yeah, well
we get to pay your fee"

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.163
and "Oh! Good for us!".

00:03:43.163 --> 00:03:45.690
We make billions of dollars
and you make your fee.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.740
- Yeah.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.870
I will say one of my favorite parts too,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.630
and I think that this gets lost sometimes.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.860
Everybody knows at this point,

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.330
Michael Jordan is Michael Jordan.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.710
He is the greatest. Right?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.000
So like everybody knows that.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.560
So, but the the point is,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.030
is that everybody doesn't know the people

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.250
behind the scenes that
made that whole brand,

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.485
that made all of that
Nike, everything come like-

00:04:04.485 --> 00:04:05.318
that's powerful.

00:04:05.318 --> 00:04:06.308
- By the way, Michael
Jordan's not in the movie

00:04:06.308 --> 00:04:07.300
on purpose.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.341
- I love that by the way!

00:04:08.341 --> 00:04:10.110
- I just thought, if you show
somebody, you try to pretend,

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.550
you tell them, this is Michael Jordan-

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.200
because he's so iconic and means so much,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.340
immediately you know it's a lie.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.780
Immediately the movie fall apart.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.030
And what's more interesting
is that the way our heroes,

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.280
these gods, kind of
operate in our lives is not

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.050
in our day-to-day lives, but we see them.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:24.540
You see him on footage in game films.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.280
But you know, they're not in real life.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.930
They're larger than life.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.330
And the audience brings their
imagination and memory to it.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.370
And it's, you know, I do really think

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.960
it's my favorite movie I've ever made.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.860
Viola Davis is amazing, Julius Tennon,

00:04:37.181 --> 00:04:38.475
Jason Bateman, Chris Tucker.

00:04:38.475 --> 00:04:39.525
- [Kelly] The cast is incredible!

00:04:39.525 --> 00:04:40.590
- These are brilliant-
they did a great job.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.420
I just watched- I'm so proud of it.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.778
It really is fun.

00:04:43.778 --> 00:04:45.003
- [Kelly] The writing is incredible.

00:04:45.003 --> 00:04:46.112
- It really should be seen in a theater.

00:04:46.112 --> 00:04:46.945
It's a lot of fun in a theater.

00:04:46.945 --> 00:04:48.600
April 5th, check it out.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.700
- It's so good. I literally
have told everyone-

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.430
I literally went to a show,
I did this show last night

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.340
and I walked in and like,
now my eyes go to Jordans.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.077
And so I'm like, and I
walked in, I was like,

00:04:59.077 --> 00:05:00.960
"Oh my God, you're gonna love the movie."

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.099
I'm like your street team.

00:05:03.099 --> 00:05:04.110
I'm like, everywhere I go, like literally.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.300
And then I had conversations
with everybody about this movie

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.100
and I'm like, they're like,
"Okay, should I see it?"

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.810
I was like, you should 100% see it!

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.070
I was like, it's so good!

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:12.720
- The beginning of shoe culture.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:13.553
- I know!

00:05:13.553 --> 00:05:14.590
- This is the very first time.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:15.918
- That's a whole thing too, yeah.

00:05:15.918 --> 00:05:17.640
It like- it ignited this whole-

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.790
my closet is mainly
sneakers. Like I love it.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.740
Like I think a lot of us are like that.

